==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhaːva/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|aːva|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hafa|lang=non}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|hafði|haft}}
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[have]]{{jump|is|have|s}}
#: ''Ég '''hef''' [[kaka#Icelandic|köku]].''
#:: I '''have''' a [[cake]].
#: ''Þú '''hefur''' [[sterkur|sterka]] [[handleggur|handleggi]].''
#:: You '''have''' [[strong]] [[arm]]s.
#: ''Skólinn '''hefur''' margt
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[hold]], to [[have]]{{jump|is|hold|s}}
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[keep]]{{jump|is|keep|s}}
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[feel]]{{jump|is|feel|s}}
#: ''Hvernig '''hefurðu''' það?'' - ''Ég '''hef''' það fínt.''
#:: How are you '''doing'''? - I'm fine.

